      <workList xml:id="workDesc_3a6ced35">
         <work xml:id="work_d1e219216">
            <identifier label="SchW" xml:id="identifier_3ad9b027">A4:400</identifier>
            <title xml:id="title_138d3774" xml:lang="it">Sonata IV a due violini et basso</title>
            <contributor xml:id="respStmt_a6847e87">
               <persName role="composer" xml:id="persName_3ea3bf19">Johann Adolph Scheibe</persName>
            </contributor>
            <history xml:id="history_5f51315c">
               <p xml:id="idm80">The collection which included the present work has presumably been lost. It is listed in Breitkopf sales catalogue of (1762) including an incipit. The trio sonata might have been composed before 1739 when Scheibe briefly mentions having composed trios without specifying them in greater detail (cf. his autobiography in Mattheson’s <rend xml:id="idm81" fontstyle="italic">Grundlage</rend>, 1740; SchW C5:001). The other works included in the collection are sonatas by <persName xml:id="idm82" auth="VIAF" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" role="">Enderlein</persName> (no. 1), <persName xml:id="idm83" auth="VIAF" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" role="">Paganelli</persName> (no. 2), <persName xml:id="idm84" auth="VIAF" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" role="">Reuter</persName> (no. 3), <persName xml:id="idm85" auth="VIAF" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" role="">Torelli</persName> (no. 5) and <persName xml:id="idm86" auth="VIAF" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" role="">Turno</persName> (no. 6), all contemporary composers of Scheibe’s.</p>
            </history>
